          "path": "_m/x/n/0/x/sh-koku-ji-wp/monument-at-the-site-of-shokok.jpg",
          "filename": "Monument at the site of Shōkoku-ji Seven-Story Pagoda (1).jpg",
          "caption": "This is a monument marking the site of the 7-storeyed Pagoda of Shōkoku-ji. In the early Muromachi period, Ashikaga Yoshimitsu, who built Shōkoku-ji, constructed a giant pagoda said to be 109 meters tall, but it burned down shortly after due to a lightning strike and no longer exists. Later on, during the final years of the Tokugawa shogunate (Keiō era), Saigō Takamori lived here, and in the late Meiji period, the family of Hideki Yukawa (whose family name at birth was Ogawa) lived here as well.",
